## Why This Is Asked

Tests a beginner KCNA candidate's ability to implement a time-window join across topics, with late data, offset handling, and at-least-once guarantees. It requires simple in-memory state management, per-key routing, and clear API boundaries.

## Key Concepts

- Time-window joins across topics
- Late-arriving data handling
- Per-message offset tracking
- Idempotent emissions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation sketch for in-memory join
class JoinEnricher {
  constructor() {
    this.latestAnnotation = new Map(); // serviceId -> { annotation, ts }
    this.metricBuffer = new Map(); // serviceId -> [{metric, ts}]
  }
  processMetric(metric, offset, ts) {
    const ann = this.latestAnnotation.get(metric.serviceId);
    const enriched = ann ? { ...metric, annotation: ann.annotation } : { ...metric, annotation: null };
    this.emitEnriched(enriched, offset);
  }
  processAnnotation(ann, offset, ts) {
    this.latestAnnotation.set(ann.serviceId, { annotation: ann.value, ts });
    // re-emit any buffered metrics for this service
    const buffered = this.metricBuffer.get(ann.serviceId) || [];
    for (const m of buffered) {
      this.emitEnriched({ ...m.metric, annotation: ann.value }, m.offset);
    }
    this.metricBuffer.set(ann.serviceId, []);
  }
  emitEnriched(record, offset) {
    // send to metrics_enriched and commit offset afterward
  }
}
```

